{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"deceitful-flannel-jerboa","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Problem\nA plan-review finding, once emitted, can be replayed verbatim on every subsequent review of the ticket even after the plan is edited to fully address it. Observed on epic 0e68-41eb-5782-4336 (outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast), 2026-08-13: the G6 finding 'the multi-project inbound fetch child does not address the three per-project enrichment passes (get_parent_map/get_comment_map/get_issuelinks_map)' was emitted BYTE-IDENTICAL — same prose, same location string, same validity 0.8889, same priority 0.8889, empty evidence list — across 5 consecutive review runs, while the description was edited to explicitly name _build_snapshot iterating the configured project set for all three enrichment passes with merge semantics and test coverage. The deterministic P4 gate measured the NEW description length each round (7469 chars on the final run), proving the live material was current; the finding text never changed.\n\n## Hypothesized mechanism (verify)\nThe pipeline's recall path (findings carry '_recall: true' in some rounds) reinjects prior-sidecar findings for re-verification, and the verification pass grounds them against the CODE (cited_reference_accurate=yes because fetcher.py:593-718 exists) but never against the CURRENT plan text — so a finding whose complaint is 'the plan does not address X' is unrefutable by fixing the plan. Byte-identical validity/priority across rounds indicates scores are carried, not recomputed.\n\n## Impact\nPlan revision loops cannot converge on any ticket once a plan-shaped finding is recalled: each round costs a full LLM review (~150s, ~500k-1M input tokens) and returns the same BLOCK. Currently blocking the wildebeast epic's attestation, which blocks its 12-child claim cascade (lamprey is claim-ready and parked).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] Root cause recorded: where recall reinjects findings and why plan-text re-grounding is skipped.\n- [ ] A recalled finding whose subject plan text has materially changed since its origin sidecar is re-grounded against the CURRENT plan text before it can block (re-verified or dropped-for-restate, whichever the design chooses) — demonstrated by a regression test.\n- [ ] Fresh findings are unaffected (a genuinely unaddressed gap still blocks).\n- [ ] Live validation: rebar review-plan 0e68-41eb-5782-4336 no longer emits the enrichment finding against the current description (which addresses it), and the review converges to a signable verdict absent other genuine findings.","id":"a43a-633e-59e5-4829","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Recalled plan-review findings never re-grounded against current plan text"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786613561295617001,"uuid":"fe1090d4-1946-4e17-9ea7-5270ab05e39f"}